#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128888 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "b0707ce1-a0fe-5749-9742-4768621332a1" :question/math-academy-id "e-5605" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/cd09988206ce7738d335cf25814f9820d5003c286904c8e136e55724f2fc1185.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-3\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-3,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/9bd0bffeaccd9f7523829b9f385c5e75a25ecd663877f0b5711d271938e484e6.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/0683c697abc42c91bc62d5f52aafa1fd7b79cd5156e999b3aac4802d9359773e.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =1,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/816a9a9b4948cae2d5a21b6e5ccf80928cadefb4d8a7ca1d333166b2fe66e5ac.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/491ab9ee9c59586dbccb6c043a3225adc3ef95496c056d37891594513f1f6069.png)\n\nTherefore, we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/6c51e641ebd7c4e64366c23aa9c7e091c3b711724069b47b104dc6f1c588f7bc.png)\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $\\mathbf{x}(t) = E\\mathbf{u}(t),$ or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=4{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=3{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128889 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/id #uuid "58c1b360-e67c-5074-919b-18fb5dbab146" :question/math-academy-id "e-5606" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=3.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/39f5b156a53392174c4b0c490f01c7bb3fee6530fc5f1e2e16be43d0de99067b.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-1\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-1,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/62cc97bb07ba88adc4b9fc6b42f33c924bf8d1d38c38ecf29973264c6ac24ee2.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/96afd68567ff82d1a461ad2b38f9492f644982f7dc4628526945bd619335c5ff.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =3,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/27f4874dc20e09331a89c5135dcacff5d6cce93d6040fdac954845478324b58b.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/6d3732ee67364278140c7e9ba5ec791cef69f4a60c8533d1f528c4bb5e718a35.png)\n\nThus, the general solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128917 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "c7bde1c8-25e8-5573-9ac4-feedd40e122f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5974" :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/72d318ad7ca3ea0dff8b598a3c7126fd48a48f25fb6bdfec859e91701ffb9d15.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/75c63b77244e0233dd11874e55a1ab674f6149d49b8fdd3c939afa1cf016ca6e.png) be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=2,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}, {\\color{blue}\\lambda_2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1{\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1} e^{{\\color{red}\\lambda_1} t} + c_2{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} e^{{\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} t}, \\qquad c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88936f10-cb2d-5f3c-bcbb-4030b7774080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354885} {:answer/id #uuid "cef1a057-a84d-5c35-a381-cae8d54808f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354886} {:answer/id #uuid "33668bb3-872a-5ff7-aa5a-760f6565f65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{1}t}+3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354887} {:answer/id #uuid "a0c43dd3-7032-5f5a-b1de-4322a535d2d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354888} {:answer/id #uuid "290f1df0-e6f4-5176-8a6d-470b27c399bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cef1a057-a84d-5c35-a381-cae8d54808f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354886} :answer-field/id #uuid "da1105ce-b427-5049-9ae4-eeddf2335b65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2917c7a7-21cc-5a74-85a9-3074d32c8f4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-168497" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84fe455a-e2af-56cc-a4ff-8dfc46b29528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354892} {:answer/id #uuid "88d78df3-79ff-55be-9362-d175fc241547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354893} {:answer/id #uuid "20c7807c-fc02-547e-a25e-272ead016d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354894} {:answer/id #uuid "bbbdaae2-189a-5d05-b3a0-21825d40907e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=c[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,c\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354895} {:answer/id #uuid "3f05139e-d8f5-54a9-85b6-6d1ffa7c234b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=4[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{1}t}+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{{c}_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354896}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20c7807c-fc02-547e-a25e-272ead016d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354894} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a544031-303f-5a9f-8774-a4259cae69a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e7beb869-f92b-5876-8cc3-7148caaba07a" :question/math-academy-id "q-168498" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129522 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704cb68f-5c4d-52bc-801a-3315a1fd0afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354898} {:answer/id #uuid "599e93ee-258b-50be-8b5b-83ece2e686b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354899} {:answer/id #uuid "5b6e7d8c-5f05-582b-8128-272160cad30e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354900} {:answer/id #uuid "71ee33a8-7046-5f56-accf-994ed378fdf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354901} {:answer/id #uuid "310a8d85-f17b-58b7-8c55-bb995adeca16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71ee33a8-7046-5f56-accf-994ed378fdf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354901} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e0490a-c124-5a24-8d42-0ad6ee6f1b4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b78e718-c7bd-590c-b65a-fabb1ffe4981" :question/math-academy-id "q-324453" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354903 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a9ef701-2dd3-5a96-9a1c-6cf2ceb4723d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354905} {:answer/id #uuid "d55841d2-9490-511e-8f26-15720ba9a80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354906} {:answer/id #uuid "b3b334e2-f5f5-53c6-8706-bc52f2582c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354907} {:answer/id #uuid "c8caa4cd-9082-5d3e-9037-a0445f7f4175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354908} {:answer/id #uuid "0fee2209-3715-52a0-8549-04880d36d07e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3b334e2-f5f5-53c6-8706-bc52f2582c1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354907} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a45ab0e-950e-5306-9f78-80f1bfba7b84" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f366a06e-f865-5088-af68-8b185629ef42" :question/math-academy-id "q-327972" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v