d/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f136251-509a-5d15-b3e3-6af4ec55c9af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354927} :answer-field/id #uuid "26bf890f-4ff0-5244-b0db-b307672b514d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354925}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "802d5442-1f0e-583f-84f8-0e38794c6ba9" :question/math-academy-id "q-327985" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1.$*" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-4\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "118cf61b-e642-5edb-a89c-b2880d26eb9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354933} {:answer/id #uuid "e77ddda6-34a0-5cf6-917c-e57aacfccf3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354934} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6f4873-ea57-5609-acea-4d14129ab843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354935} {:answer/id #uuid "10d5a617-ae80-54b3-a57d-a4e0bf311386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354936} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ec945e-3519-52f9-be9c-a0a7c5e0668f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab6f4873-ea57-5609-acea-4d14129ab843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354935} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee402a1-e0a2-5ca9-abc4-4a19a26a6f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b130cbca-fb25-5b40-a5cd-8a57800c8968" :question/math-academy-id "q-327995" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c65d59ff-12bd-53c0-aaa0-9321c981191c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354940} {:answer/id #uuid "36c8f169-d1a5-59a4-8b2e-8e973aaf3d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354941} {:answer/id #uuid "1cffb798-db0a-5a84-9d2b-629e407a7d27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354942} {:answer/id #uuid "fee110ee-6556-59ed-8d10-a55791b654b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354943} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b51f3c-8225-583c-8cce-232156a59797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6b51f3c-8225-583c-8cce-232156a59797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354944} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa6e2baa-8a1e-5418-bb23-7a1c54ecd2d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354939}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f0bc18c-9cad-5fa9-b040-3bff4cc9faa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-327997" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354945 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2692c169-681b-5cd1-816e-d524e5e82979" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354947} {:answer/id #uuid "39cd13ca-b0e2-511b-a50a-a40be01e5e50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354948} {:answer/id #uuid "4298549d-f15e-5e96-b7a9-80c328d38381" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354949} {:answer/id #uuid "826d5ec3-0fbb-51ca-98ce-94136c26a92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354950} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa64c7d-e1d2-540b-ba93-6ce59a84b434" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "826d5ec3-0fbb-51ca-98ce-94136c26a92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354950} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd7b197-a9e0-56a3-a34d-eda7c0d54092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354946}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88f4bcdc-08ae-5cd3-83e3-4ae7b98eda2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-327999" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Decoupling Substitution of a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71830596-5160-5f30-abf6-2ebce447c516" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354954} {:answer/id #uuid "4b30e091-5ef6-5b9c-817a-19be1a86f57c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354955} {:answer/id #uuid "1cd77233-04e1-5b99-a546-a947864d2dc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354956} {:answer/id #uuid "87f69981-7b79-5845-870b-409559b440a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354957} {:answer/id #uuid "709f9a42-56e4-5889-aa47-da5d98b00cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "709f9a42-56e4-5889-aa47-da5d98b00cc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354958} :answer-field/id #uuid "d443d88f-d41e-5f52-8174-d04982c0be18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "547cf423-346c-5ea7-9462-268138005651" :question/math-academy-id "q-39699" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126ddc63-27b9-5f21-9e25-a088a505a824" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354960} {:answer/id #uuid "a462c7a0-0534-57f7-a3bc-43a0e1fc8b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354961} {:answer/id #uuid "26e0e239-fa4f-515f-ae03-472fe991bf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354962} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7e29c3-df05-5e78-9b60-5d512b0e0efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354963} {:answer/id #uuid "829d1a12-25cb-5ff3-b53b-75d29b743d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354964}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26e0e239-fa4f-515f-ae03-472fe991bf45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354962} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c6a1718-a91b-5bb7-a7f1-40d48b2d9656" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5a748532-336b-52f0-98a1-66ff075744fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-39700" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{0t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "16d1e71b-6eda-5c91-81a0-15a1aa979932" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution Given the Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors of the Corresponding Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99e2e2b2-3641-5b0f-9dd0-15768bb938e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354967} {:answer/id #uuid "30d4fffe-1003-5c75-883d-5357ef1a87ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354968} {:answer/id #uuid "d6f5e2b2-3f42-5621-95fd-62ed584ead8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354969} {:answer/id #uuid "63ca239a-66a1-5756-8d20-7173541ca4a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1